&Q000396 = A praise poem of Šulgi (Šulgi B)
@composite
#project: etcslatf/inter
#atf: use unicode
#atf: use math
#etcsl: text-id=c.2.4.2.02
#key: after http://etcsl.orinst.ox.ac.uk/cgi-bin/etcsl.cgi?text=c.2.4.2.02&display=Crit&charenc=gcirc#

1. lugal-e mu-ni niŋ₂-ul-še₃
#lem: lugal[king]; mu[name]; niŋul[an everlasting thing]
#tr.en: To make his name famous for all time until distant days, 
#etcsl: line-id=1

#etcsl#cite Cited in OB catalogue from Nibru, at Philadelphia, 0.2.01, line 26; OB catalogue in the Louvre, 0.2.02, line 17; OB catalogue from Urim (U1), 0.2.03, line 1, line 13

2. ud su₃-ra₂-ka pa e₃ ak-de₃
#lem: ud[sun]; sud[distant]; pa[branch]; e[leave]; ak[do]
#tr.en: and to transmit to posterity and the days  
#etcsl: line-id=2

3. {d}šul-gi lugal urim₅{ki}-ma-ke₄
#lem: Šulgir[1]RN; lugal[king]; Urim[1]SN
#tr.en: to come the praise poems of his power, 
#etcsl: line-id=3

4. a₂-na za₃-mi₂-bi-im kalag-ga-na šir₃-bi-im
#lem: a[arm]; zamin[praise]; kalag[strong]; šir[song]
#tr.en: the songs of his might, 
#etcsl: line-id=4

5. gal-an-zu niŋ₂ saŋ-bi-še₃ e₃-a-na mu da-ri₂-bi-im
#lem: galanzu[wise]; niŋ[thing]; saŋ[head]; e[leave]; mu[name]; dari[eternal]
#tr.en: and the lasting fame of his exceptional intelligence, 
#etcsl: line-id=5

6. šag₄-bal-bal-a eŋer ud-da-ka šu-a bal-e-de₃
#lem: šabalbal[descendent]; egir[back]; ud[sun]; šu[hand]; bala[turn]
#tr.en: King @wRN{Šulgi}, 
#etcsl: line-id=6

7. kalag-ga dumu {d}nin-sumun₂-ka-ra
#lem: kalag[strong]; dumu[child]; Ninsumunak[1]DN
#tr.en: king of @wSN{Urim}, 
#etcsl: line-id=7

8. ŋeštug₂ egir-ra-bi igi-še₃ mu-un-na-de₆
#lem: ŋeštug[ear]; egir[back]; igi[eye]; de[carry]
#tr.en: has brought the songs' latent wisdom before the mighty son of @wDN{Ninsumun}. 
#etcsl: line-id=8

9. a₂-ni šir₃-ra silim-eš₂ mu-un-e
#lem: a[arm]; šir[song]; silim[healthy]; dug[speak]
#tr.en: He praises his own power in song, 
#etcsl: line-id=9

10. dim₂-ma niŋ₂ sag₉-ga šag₄-ta DU-a-ni ni₂-bi i₃-buluŋ₅-e
#lem: dimma[thought]; niŋ[thing]; sag[good]; šag[heart]; X; ni[self]; buluŋ[grow]
#tr.en: and lauds his own superior native intelligence: 
#etcsl: line-id=10

11. lugal a lugal-e ru-a nin-e tud-da-me-en
#lem: lugal[king]; a[water]; lugal[king]; ri[impose]; nin[lady]; utud[give birth (to)]
#tr.en: I am a king, offspring begotten by a king and borne by a queen. 
#etcsl: line-id=11

12. {d}šul-gi-me-en dumu-gir₁₅ šag₄ zid-ta nam dug₃ tar-ra-me-en
#lem: Šulgir[1]RN; dumugir[citizen]; šag[heart]; zid[right]; nam[fate]; dug[good]; tar[cut]
#tr.en: I, @wRN{Šulgi} the noble, 
#etcsl: line-id=12

13. tur-ra-ŋu₁₀-ne e₂-dub-ba-a-a-am₃
#lem: tur[small]; edubbaʾa[scribal school]
#tr.en: have been blessed with a favourable destiny right from the womb. 
#etcsl: line-id=13

14. dub ki-en-gi ki-uri-ka nam-dub-sar-ra mi-ni-zu
#lem: dub[tablet]; Kengir[1]; Akkad[1 Akkad]; namdubsar[the scribal arts]; zu[know]
#tr.en: When I was small, I was at the academy, 
#etcsl: line-id=14

15. nam-dumu-gir₁₅ ŋe₂₆-e-gin₇-nam im nu-mu-un-sar
#lem: namdumugir[citizen status]; ŋaʾe[I]; im[clay]; sar[write]
#tr.en: where I learned the scribal art from the tablets of @wGN{Sumer} and @wGN{Akkad}. 
#etcsl: line-id=15

16. nam-dub-sar-ra ki nam-kug-zu-ba lu₂ im-mi-re₆-re₆
#lem: namdubsar[the scribal arts]; ki[place]; namkugzu[wisdom]; lu[person]; ere[go (perfect plural stem of ŋen⟦to go⟧)]
#tr.en: None of the nobles could write on clay as I could. 
#etcsl: line-id=16

17. zi-zi-i ŋa₂-ŋa₂ šudum niŋ₂-šid-de₃ zag im-mi-til-til
#lem: zig[rise]; ŋar[put]; šudum[reckoning]; niŋkas[account]; zag[side]; til[complete]
#tr.en: There where people regularly went for tutelage in the scribal art, 

#etcsl: line-id=17

18. {d}nanibgal sig₇-ga {d}nisaba₂-ke₄
#lem: Nanibgal[1]DN; sissig[green-yellow]; Nisabak[1]DN
#tr.en: I qualified fully in subtraction, addition, reckoning and accounting. The fair @wDN{Nanibgal}, 
#etcsl: line-id=18

19. ŋeštug₂ ŋizzal₂-la šu daŋal ma-ni-in-dug₄
#lem: ŋeštug[ear]; ŋizzal[hearing]; šu[hand]; daŋal[wide]; dug[speak]
#tr.en: @wDN{Nisaba}, provided me amply with knowledge and comprehension. 
#etcsl: line-id=19

20. dub-sar ŋal₂ taka₄-a niŋ₂-e nu-dib-be₂-me-en
#lem: dubsar[scribe]; ŋal[open]; taka[set aside]; niŋ[thing]; dib[pass]
#tr.en: I am an experienced scribe who does not neglect a thing. 
#etcsl: line-id=20

21. sa nemur₂(|PIRIG.TUR|)-gin₇ zig₃-ga-ŋu₁₀-ne
#lem: sa[sinew]; nemur[leopard]; zig[rise]
#tr.en: When I sprang up, 
#etcsl: line-id=21

22. {anše}niskum(PIRIG)-gin₇ kaš₄ kalag-ga di-ŋa₂
#lem: nisku[description of equids]; kaš[run]; kalag[strong]; di[speak]
#tr.en: muscular as a cheetah, 
#etcsl: line-id=22

23. šag₄ an-na-ke₄ hul₂-la ma-ab-de₆
#lem: šag[heart]; An[1]DN; hul[rejoice]; de[carry]
#tr.en: galloping like a thoroughbred ass at full gallop, 
#etcsl: line-id=23

24. a-la-ŋa₂ {d}en-lil₂-le gu₃ zid ma-ni-in-de₂
#lem: ala[exuberance]; Enlil[1]DN; gu[voice]; zid[right]; de[pour]
#tr.en: the favour of @wDN{An} brought me joy; 
#etcsl: line-id=24

25. nam-si-sa₂-ŋu₁₀-uš ŋidru ma-an-šum₂-mu-uš
#lem: namsisa[justness]; ŋidru[scepter]; šum[give]
#tr.en: to my delight @wDN{Enlil} spoke favourably about me, 
#etcsl: line-id=25

26. gu₂ kur-kur-ra-ka ŋiri₃ ba-da-gub
#lem: gu[neck]; kur[mountain(s)]; ŋiri[foot]; gub[stand]
#tr.en: and they gave me the sceptre because of my righteousness. 
#etcsl: line-id=26

27. {ŋiš}tukul-ŋa₂ mu-bi sig-še₃ mu-un-ŋal₂
#lem: tukul[weapon]; mu[name]; sig[weak]; ŋal[⟦be⟧ to be (there]
#tr.en: I place my foot on the neck of the foreign lands; 
#etcsl: line-id=27

28. aga₃-kar₂ sig₁₀-ga-ŋu₁₀ igi-nim-še₃ mu-un-ŋal₂
#lem: agakar[conquest]; sig[put into]; iginim[upper land]; ŋal[⟦be⟧ to be (there]
#tr.en: the fame of my weapons is established as far as the south, 
#etcsl: line-id=28

29. me₃ šen-šen-na um-ta-ab-e₃-en
#lem: me[battle]; šen[battle]; e[leave]
#tr.en: and my victory is established in the highlands. 
#etcsl: line-id=29

30. ki ib₂-dug₄-ga {d}en-lil₂-la₂-še₃
#lem: ki[place]; dug[speak]; Enlil[1]DN
#tr.en: When I set off for battle and strife to a place that @wDN{Enlil} has commanded me, 
#etcsl: line-id=30

31. ama erin₂-na-ŋu₁₀-u₈ igi-še₃ ba-du-un
#lem: ama[mother]; erin[people]; igi[eye]; du[go]
#tr.en: I go ahead of the main body of my troops and I clear the terrain for my scouts. 
#etcsl: line-id=31

32. igi-bar-ra-ŋu₁₀-u₈ a-šag₄ ba-ab-zalag-ge-en
#lem: igibarra[scout]; ašag[field]; zalag[bright]
#tr.en: I have a positive passion for weapons. 
#etcsl: line-id=32

33. ŋe₂₆-e-me-en {ŋiš}tukul-la a-la mu-un-ŋa₂-ŋa₂-an
#lem: ŋaʾe[I]; tukul[weapon]; ala[exuberance]; ŋar[put]
#tr.en: Not only do I carry lance and spear, 
#etcsl: line-id=33

34. {urud}šukur {urud}ma-sa-tum a-ba-da-ab-ŋal₂-le-en-na
#lem: šukur[lance]; masatum[lance?]; ŋal[⟦be⟧ to be (there]
#tr.en: I also know how to handle slingstones with a sling. 
#etcsl: line-id=34

35. {kuš}da-lu-uš₂-a a₂-sag₃-ge-bi mu-zu
#lem: daluš[sling]; asig[slingstone]; zu[know]
#tr.en: The clay bullets, 
#etcsl: line-id=35

36. im-dug im-lag hul sag₃-ga-ŋu₁₀
#lem: imdug[clay sling shot]; imlag[pellet]; hulu[bad]; sag[strike]
#tr.en: the treacherous pellets that I shoot, 
#etcsl: line-id=36

37. mir im ne₃-ŋal₂-la-gin₇ dal-le-da-bi
#lem: mir[north wind]; im[rain]; neŋal[mighty]; dal[fly]
#tr.en: fly around like a violent rainstorm. 
#etcsl: line-id=37

38. šag₄ dab-ba-ŋu₁₀-u₈ la-ba-ab-dib-be₂-en
#lem: šag[heart]; dab[seize]; dib[pass]
#tr.en: In my rage I do not let them miss. 
#etcsl: line-id=38

39. ni₂ zi ir kur-re ba-ab-šum₂-mu-un
#lem: ni[fear]; zi[life]; ir[cvve]; kur[mountain(s)]; šum[give]
#tr.en: I sow fear and confusion in the foreign land. 
#etcsl: line-id=39

40. šeš gu₅-li-ŋu₁₀ šul {d}utu-am₃
#lem: šeš[brother]; guli[friend]; šul[youth]; Utu[1]DN
#tr.en: I look to my brother and friend, youthful @wDN{Utu}, 
#etcsl: line-id=40

41. ki zi-šag₄-ŋal₂-la-ka igi mu-na-ni-du₈
#lem: ki[place]; zišagŋal[encouragement]; igi[eye]; du[spread]
#tr.en: as a source of divine encouragement. I, @wRN{Šulgi}, converse with him whenever he rises over there; 
#etcsl: line-id=41

42. {d}šul-gi-me-en dalla e₃-bi-a inim mu-un-da-bal-e-en
#lem: Šulgir[1]RN; dalla[(to be) bright]; e[leave]; inim[word]; bala[turn]
#tr.en: he is the god who keeps a good eye on my battles. 
#etcsl: line-id=42

43. diŋir igi sag₉ me₃-ŋa₂-a-kam
#lem: diŋir[deity]; igi[eye]; sag[goodness]; me[battle]
#tr.en: The youth @wDN{Utu}, beloved in the mountains, is the protective deity of my weapons; 
#etcsl: line-id=43

44. šul {d}utu kur-ra ki aŋ₂ {d}lamma {ŋiš}tukul-ŋa₂-kam
#lem: šul[youth]; Utu[1]DN; kur[mountain(s)]; ki[place]; aŋ[measure]; lammar[(female) tutelary deity]; tukul[weapon]
#tr.en: by his words I am strengthened and made pugnacious (?). 
#etcsl: line-id=44

45. inim-ma-ni-še₃ ga-mu-un-kalag-ge LA ga-mu-un-ne₃-e
#lem: inim[word]; kalag[strong]; X; e[speak]
#tr.en: In those battles, 
#etcsl: line-id=45

46. me₃ ŋiš ŋiš-e la₂-a-ba {d}utu ŋa₂-a-ar ma-an-e₃
#lem: me[battle]; ŋeš[tree]; ŋeš[tree]; la[hang]; Utu[1]DN; ŋaʾe[I]; e[leave]
#tr.en: where weapon clashes on weapon, 
#etcsl: line-id=46

47. {ŋiš}tukul igi-nim-ma dug₃-ŋa₂ bi₂-tar
#lem: tukul[weapon]; iginim[upper land]; dug[good]; tar[cut]
#tr.en: @wDN{Utu} shines on me. 
#etcsl: line-id=47

48. sig-še₃ elam{ki}-ma gu₃-ba ŋiš ma-ab-us₂
#lem: sig[weak]; Elam[1]GN; gu[voice]; ŋeš[tree]; us[accompany]
#tr.en: Thus I broke the weapons of the highlands over my knees, 
#etcsl: line-id=48

49. ki-bal {ŋiš}tukul-ŋa₂ a-na ba-zig₃-zig₃-ga
#lem: kibala[rebel land]; tukul[weapon]; ana[what?]; zig[rise]
#tr.en: and in the south placed a yoke on the neck of @wGN{Elam}. 
#etcsl: line-id=49

50. nam-lu₂-ulu₃-bi še sahar-ra-gin₇
#lem: namlulu[humanity]; še[barley]; sahar[soil]
#tr.en: I make the populations of the rebel lands -- how could they still resist my weapons? 
#etcsl: line-id=50

51. ki-en-gi ki-uri ha-ba-ni-du₈
#lem: Kengir[1]; Akkad[1 Akkad]; du[spread]
#tr.en: -- scatter like seed-grain over @wGN{Sumer} and @wGN{Akkad}. 
#etcsl: line-id=51

52. niŋ₂ ak-a-ŋa₂ ni₂-bi ga-buluŋ₅
#lem: niŋ[thing]; ak[do]; ni[self]; buluŋ[grow]
#tr.en: Let me boast of what I have done. 
#etcsl: line-id=52

53. kalag-ga-ŋa₂ mu-bi a₂ bi₂-su₃-ud
#lem: kalag[strong]; mu[name]; a[arm]; sud[distant]
#tr.en: The fame of my power is spread far and wide. 
#etcsl: line-id=53

54. ŋeštug₂-ŋu₁₀ niŋ₂ galam-ma sug₄-ga-am₃
#lem: ŋeštug[ear]; niŋ[thing]; galam[skilful]; sug[full]
#tr.en: My wisdom is full of subtlety. 
#etcsl: line-id=54

55. a-na-ŋu₁₀ niŋ₂ ka-ge dib-ba nu
#lem: ana[what?]; niŋ[thing]; kag[mouth]; dib[pass]; nu[not]
#tr.en: Do not my achievements surpass all qualifications? 
#etcsl: line-id=55

56. nam-nun-da du-du-a-ŋu₁₀-ne
#lem: namnun[magnificence]; du[go]
#tr.en: I stride forward in majesty, trampling endlessly through the esparto grass and thickets, 
#etcsl: line-id=56

57. {u₂}numun₂ ŋiš hul {u₂}numun₂ ŋiš hul zukum-ma-ŋu₁₀-ne
#lem: numun[alfalfa grass]; ŋeš[tree]; hulu[bad]; numun[alfalfa grass]; ŋeš[tree]; hulu[bad]; zukum[tread]
#tr.en: capturing elephant after elephant, creatures of the plain; 
#etcsl: line-id=57

58. til-lu-ug til-lu-ug-da niŋ₂-zi-ŋal₂ edin-na dab₅-dab₅-be₂-da-ŋu₁₀-ne
#lem: tillug[elephant]; tillug[elephant]; niŋziŋal[living creature]; eden[steppe]; dab[seize]
#tr.en: and I put an end to the heroic roaring in the plains of the different liona, 
#etcsl: line-id=58

59. ur-mah ug ušumgal eden-na-ke₄
#lem: urmah[lion]; ug[lion]; ušumgal[great dragon]; eden[steppe]
#tr.en: the dragons of the plains, 
#etcsl: line-id=59

60. me-da im-ti-ba me-a ŋen-na-ba
#lem: meta[where from? whence?]; teŋ[approach]; mea[where?]; ŋen[go]
#tr.en: wherever it approaches from and wherever it is going. 
#etcsl: line-id=60

61. gu₃ nam-ur-saŋ-ŋa₂-bi-ir edin-na ŋa₂-la ha-ba-ni-dag-dag
#lem: gu[voice]; namursaŋ[heroism]; eden[back]; ŋala[cvne]; dag[roam around]
#tr.en: I do not go after them with a net, 
#etcsl: line-id=61

62. sa-du₃-a-ta ba-ra-ab-ši-ŋen-ne-en
#lem: sadu[net]; ŋen[go]
#tr.en: nor do I lie in wait for them in a hide; 
#etcsl: line-id=62

63. še-er-tab-ta en-nu-uŋ₃ ba-ra-bi₂-ak
#lem: šertab[reed fence]; ennuŋ[watch]; ak[do]
#tr.en: it comes to a confrontation of strength and weapons. 
#etcsl: line-id=63

64. a₂ ŋiš-la₂-a ba-ab-ak {ŋiš}tukul ba-ra-bi₂-šub{ub}
#lem: a[arm]; ŋešla[battle]; ak[do]; tukul[weapon]; šub[fall]
#tr.en: I do not hurl a weapon; 
#etcsl: line-id=64

65. ud zu₂ sis-a-bi {urud}šukur zi-ba he₂-bi₂-ŋar
#lem: ud[sun]; zu[tooth]; ses[bitter]; šukur[lance]; zi[life]; ŋar[put]
#tr.en: when I plunge a bitter-pointed lance in their throats, 
#etcsl: line-id=65

66. za-pa-aŋ₂-bi-še₃ gaba-ŋu₁₀ ba-ra-bi₂-zig₃
#lem: zipaŋ[voice]; gaba[breast]; zig[rise]
#tr.en: I do not flinch at their roar. 
#etcsl: line-id=66

67. ŋe₂₆-e tuš-ŋu₁₀-še₃ ba-ra-ba-ta-ŋen-ne-en
#lem: ŋaʾe[I]; tuš[sit (down)]; ŋen[go]
#tr.en: I am not one to retreat to my hiding-place but, 
#etcsl: line-id=67

68. ur-saŋ ur-saŋ-e gaz-a-gin₇
#lem: ursaŋ[warrior]; ursaŋ[warrior]; gaz[kill]
#tr.en: as when one warrior kills another warrior, I do everything swiftly on the open plain. 
#etcsl: line-id=68

69. edin-na niŋ₂ ul₄-la-aš hu-mu-ni-ak
#lem: eden[back]; niŋ[thing]; ul[hasten]; ak[do]
#tr.en: In the desert where the paths peter out, 
#etcsl: line-id=69

70. gu₃ šubtum₅-ma ki ŋiri₃ kud-da-ba edin-ba hu-mu-sig₉-si-ig
#lem: gu[voice]; šubtum[dwelling]; ki[place]; ŋiri[foot]; kud[cut]; eden[back]; sig[silent]
#tr.en: I reduce the roar at the lair to silence. 
#etcsl: line-id=70

71. tur₃ amaš ki saŋ bi₂-in-bur₂-bur₂-ra
#lem: tur[animal stall]; amaš[sheepfold]; ki[place]; saŋ[head]; bur[spread out]
#tr.en: In the sheepfold and the cattle-pen, where heads are laid to rest (?), 
#etcsl: line-id=71

72. sipad ildum₂-ma-bi-ir su-bi hu-mu-dug₃
#lem: sipad[shepherd]; ildum[band]; su[flesh]; dug[good]
#tr.en: I put the shepherd tribesmen at ease. 
#etcsl: line-id=72

73. ud me-da ud ul-le₂-a-še₃
#lem: ud[sun]; meta[where from? whence?]; ud[sun]; ul[distant time]
#tr.en: Let no one ever at any time say about me, 
#etcsl: line-id=73

74. ga-nam 1(AŠ)-bi ba-an-da-sig₁₀-ga lu₂ nam-mu-un-ši-ib-be₂
#lem: ganam[moreover]; n; sig[put into]; lu[person]; e[speak]
#tr.en: @q{“Could he really subdue them all on his own?”} 
#etcsl: line-id=74

75. ur-mah {ŋiš}tukul-la bi₂-til-la-ŋu₁₀
#lem: urmah[lion]; tukul[weapon]; til[complete]
#tr.en: The number of lions that I have despatched with my weapons is limitless; 
#etcsl: line-id=75

76. a-ra₂-bi zag-bi-še₃ šid-bi ba-ra-zu
#lem: ara[times (with numbers)]; zag[side]; šid[count]; zu[know]
#tr.en: their total is unknown. 
#etcsl: line-id=76

77. niŋ₂ ak-a-ŋa₂ ni₂-bi ga-buluŋ₅
#lem: niŋ[thing]; ak[do]; ni[self]; buluŋ[grow]
#tr.en: Let me boast of what I have done. 
#etcsl: line-id=77

78. kalag-ga-ŋa₂ mu-bi a₂ bi₂-su₃-ud
#lem: kalag[strong]; mu[name]; a[arm]; sud[distant]
#tr.en: The fame of my power is spread far and wide. 
#etcsl: line-id=78

79. ŋeštug₂-ŋu₁₀ niŋ₂ galam-ma sug₄-ga-am₃
#lem: ŋeštug[ear]; niŋ[thing]; galam[skilful]; sug[full]
#tr.en: My wisdom is full of subtlety. 
#etcsl: line-id=79

80. a-na-ŋu₁₀ niŋ₂ ka-ge dib-ba nu
#lem: ana[what?]; niŋ[thing]; kag[mouth]; dib[pass]; nu[not]
#tr.en: Do not my achievements surpass all qualifications? 
#etcsl: line-id=80

81. {d}šul-gi diŋir nam-ŋuruš-a saŋ-kal erin₂-na-me-en
#lem: Šulgir[1]RN; diŋir[deity]; namŋuruš[manliness]; saŋkal[foremost]; erin[people]
#tr.en: I am @wRN{Šulgi}, god of manliness, the foremost of the troops. 
#etcsl: line-id=81

82. tir-ra sa i-ni-sa₂ ti galam-ma i-ni-gid₂
#lem: tir[bow]; sa[sinew]; sa[equal]; ti[arrow]; galam[skilful]; gid[long]
#tr.en: When I stretch the bowstring on the bow, when I fit a perfect arrow to it, 
#etcsl: line-id=82

83. niŋ₂ šu min₃ a₂-ta ri-a-ŋa₂ {ŋiš}gag-pan he₂-ni-ib-ri-en
#lem: niŋ[thing]; šu[hand]; n; a[arm]; ri[impose]; kakpana[arrow]; ri[impose]
#tr.en: I shoot the bow's arrow with the full strength of my arms. 
#etcsl: line-id=83

84. am gal gud an-na sumun₂ alim gu₃ ib₂-de₂-de₂-e
#lem: am[wild bull]; gal[big]; gud[bull]; an[sky]; sumun[wild cow]; alim[bison]; gu[voice]; de[pour]
#tr.en: The great wild bull, the bull of heaven, the wild cow and the bison bellow. 
#etcsl: line-id=84

